+# Copyright 2026 Observational Health Data Sciences and Informatics
+# Licensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0.
+
+#' Stepwise sparse logistic coordinate descent
+#'
+#' Initialize and advance the existing CPU Cyclops CCD calculation without
+#' running a local fit. Only unweighted, float64 binary logistic regression
+#' with one unpenalized intercept and independent Laplace priors is supported.
+#'
+#' @param y Named numeric binary outcome vector.
+#' @param sx A \code{dgCMatrix} without an intercept. Its unique row names must
+#'   equal \code{names(y)} in order. Column names must be unique and nonempty.
+#'   Empty local columns are retained; a global zero column cannot be updated.
+#' @param prior A fixed-variance \code{createPrior("laplace")} object, excluding
+#'   only \code{"(Intercept)"}.
+#' @param control A \code{createControl()} object using \code{algorithm="ccd"},
+#'   \code{convergenceType="lange"}, one CPU thread and no screening.
+#' @param startingCoefficients Finite numeric coefficients named exactly
+#'   \code{c("(Intercept)", colnames(sx))}, including the intercept.
+#' @param object The \code{cyclopsData} environment returned by initialization.
+#' @param covariate The name of the next coordinate, including
+#'   \code{"(Intercept)"} at the start of each sweep.
+#' @param gradient Summed derivative of the negative log likelihood.
+#' @param curvature Summed second derivative of the negative log likelihood.
+#'   It must be positive, even when a local contribution is zero.
+#' @param logLikelihood The sum of site log likelihoods at the current
+#'   coefficients. If \code{NULL}, use this object's local log likelihood.
+#'
+#' @details
+#' No normalization, feature removal, cross-validation, weighting or transport
+#' is performed. Inputs must already share a feature order and scale.
+#' The Laplace rate is \code{sqrt(2 / prior$variance)} for the summed likelihood.
+#'
+#' Call \code{checkCyclopsCoordinateConvergence()} initially and after every
+#' complete sweep. For multiple states pass the same summed log likelihood
+#' to each state. The common log prior is added internally exactly once.
+#' Statistics must be calculated at the same coefficients, summed, then
+#' applied to every state before moving to the next coordinate.
+#'
+#' Statistics retrieval leaves coefficients, bounds and predictors unchanged.
+#' Updates reuse Cyclops' Laplace increment, zero crossing, trust bounds and
